{"arrivo":"da","origine":"gml","origine_nome":"Middle Low German","livello2":"dum","livello2_nome":"Middle Dutch","n":11,"parole":[{"parola":"bakke","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"tray, salver","termine_origine":"bak","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"bak","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"bak","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"bacca","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-med","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German bak, back or Middle Dutch bak, from Medieval Latin bacca (“basin, bowl”)."},{"parola":"bøje","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"buoy","termine_origine":"boie","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"boie","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"boeye","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"fro","nome":"Old French","termine":"buie","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"frk","nome":"Frankish","termine":"*baukn","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"frk","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German boie, Middle Dutch boeye, from Old French buie (“fetter, chain”) (French bouée). This word is probably borrowed from Frankish *baukn, cognate with English beacon and Old Frisian bāken. Doublet of bavn and båke)."},{"parola":"forlis","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"loss, shipwreck (loss of a ship at sea)","termine_origine":"vorlēs","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"vorlēs","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"vorlies","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"dum","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"A verbal noun of forlise, borrowed from Middle Low German vorlēs or Middle Dutch vorlies."},{"parola":"ganske","pos":"adj|adv","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"whole, complete","termine_origine":"gans","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"gans","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"gansch","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"goh","nome":"Old High German","termine":"ganz","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*gant","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German gans or Middle Dutch gansch; both from Old High German ganz (“whole, entire, sound, complete”), from Proto-West Germanic *gant (“all, whole, complete”)."},{"parola":"knop","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"bud (of a plant)","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"knoppe","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"dum","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German and Middle Dutch knoppe; see knob."},{"parola":"kontor","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"office","termine_origine":"kontōr","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"kontōr","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"cantoor","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"frm","nome":"Middle French","termine":"contoir","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"computo","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Middle Low German kontōr (“commercial branch; writing room; counting desk”), from Middle Dutch cantoor, cantoor, from Middle French contoir, comptoir, from conter, compter (“to count”) + -oir (instrument suffix), from Latin computāre (“calculate, compute”) and -tōrium."},{"parola":"ridder","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"knight (a medieval horseman)","termine_origine":"ridder","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"ridder","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"riddere","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"dum","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German ridder (“rider, knight”), from Middle Dutch riddere, a Flemish variant of rîdere, from rîden (“to ride”) + -er. It was used to translate Old French chevalier (“knight”). The Dutch word was also borrowed to German Ritter, Old Norse riddari, and Swedish riddare."},{"parola":"skule","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps","significato":"to scowl, have an angry expression","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"schulen","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*skelhaz","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Influenced by skjule (“to conceal, hide, stare to the side”), perhaps ultimately from Middle Low German or Middle Dutch schulen (“to hide, take shelter”). Or, from Proto-Germanic *skelhaz (“squint-eyed”), related to Old English sceolh (“squinting”), Old Norse skjalgr (“squinting, askew”)."},{"parola":"tromme","pos":"noun|verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"a drum","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"tromme","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"dum","ambiti":["musica"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German or Middle Dutch tromme, of imitative origin."},{"parola":"ur","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"clock","termine_origine":"ūr","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"ūr","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"ūre","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"fro","nome":"Old French","termine":"houre","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"hōra","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"ὥρα","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German ūr (“watch, clock”), which was borrowed, via Middle Dutch ūre, from Old French houre (“hour”), from Latin hōra (“hour”) and ultimately Ancient Greek ὥρα (hṓra, “season, hour”). The German Uhr (“watch”) was also borrowed from Low German."},{"parola":"værk","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":3,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"oakum","termine_origine":"werk","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"werk","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"dum","nome":"Middle Dutch","termine":"werk","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"dum","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German werk or Middle Dutch werk, cognate with Old High German werah, werc, German Werg. Originally the same word as the first one."}]}